<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Diego de Landa</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1524">1524</a>–<a href="/years/1579">1579</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Diego de Landa was a Spanish Franciscan friar and later <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">Bishop</a> of Yucatán. In 1562 he led an inquisition against Maya converts suspected of idolatry and burnt Maya codices and images at Maní. His account of Yucatán, the Relación de las cosas de Yucatán, nevertheless became a principal source for Maya history, customs and writing, including the provinces formed after the fall of Mayapan.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/diego-de-landa.jpg" alt="Diego de Landa" width="320" height="317" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Diego_de_Landa.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
